<p><strong>A tattoo or piercing studio avoids clashes and no-show losses when each artist and piercer has a clear schedule, consultations and deposits are recorded, and every payment is tracked.</strong></p>
@NOTE@@
<h2>The long session and the walk-in piercing</h2>
<p>A six-hour back piece is booked for one artist. A walk-in wants a quick piercing, and the front desk squeezes it in. The consultation that was meant to happen is forgotten, the deposit is in someone's pocket notes, and the client who did not show up costs a full day of lost work.</p>
<h2>What goes wrong in a studio</h2>
<ul><li>Long sessions overlapped by short bookings.</li><li>Deposits and consultations kept in chats.</li><li>No-shows with nothing on record.</li></ul>
<h2>How it is solved</h2>
<p>Each booking checks the artist or piercer, room and time together, so long sessions stay protected. Deposits and part-payments are recorded against the booking with <a href="/features/payment-tracking/">payment tracking</a>. Read more on <a href="/solutions/tattoo/">software for tattoo studios</a> and the <a href="/blog/tattoo-studio-booking-and-deposits/">tattoo booking and deposits guide</a>.</p>
<h2>A quick fix you can start today</h2>
<ol><li>Take a deposit for every long session and write it down.</li><li>Keep consultations in the same schedule as sessions.</li><li>Record no-shows so you can see the pattern.</li></ol>
